        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazlet%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The township’s name comes from Dr. John Hazlett, who owned an estate near the Keyport-Holmdel Turnpike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hazlet%2C_New_Jersey"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hazlet hosted New Jersey’s last drive‑in movie theater, the Route 35 Drive‑In, which closed in 1991.",
